cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use BorderKeys in research, cite it as below."
type: software
title: "BorderKeys"
abstract: >-
  An Android keyboard that asks for no permission and opens no network connection: a compact
  trie with word pairs and triples in C++ for suggestions and corrections, a geometric and a
  neural swipe decoder, a personal dictionary and a clipboard history in an encrypted
  database, and a text assistant that runs in its own process on the device.
authors:
  - name: "BorderKeys contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/razvan-eduard/borderkeys"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
version: "0.8.0"
date-released: "2026-09-25"
keywords:
  - android
  - keyboard
  - input method
  - swipe typing
  - privacy
